jobs.description:
As a Warehouse Employee at DHL in Weert, you’ll be responsible for various logistics activities within the warehouse. Your tasks may include receiving, checking, storing, picking, and preparing goods for shipment. You’ll also work with Material Handling Equipment (MHE), such as an EPT or stacker, after receiving the appropriate training.

You’ll make sure that products are processed accurately and efficiently and that the warehouse runs smoothly. Because you’ll be working with ASML-related products, precision, responsibility, and following procedures are very important.

- You are 18 years or older (due to working hours);
- You have previous work experience in logistics, warehousing, or a similar environment;
- You’re available full-time (40 hours per week), either in two shifts or during the day;
- You’re able to request a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You have a basic understanding of English, as it is used daily in the warehouse;
- You’re eager to learn new skills, such as operating an EPT or stacker;
- You are comfortable working in a structured and fast-paced logistics environment.

Together with your colleagues, you ensure that goods are processed efficiently and accurately throughout the warehouse. You contribute to a safe and organised working environment while helping maintain a smooth flow of products.

• Loading and unloading trucks;
• Sorting goods and shipments;
• Picking orders;
• Packing and preparing orders for shipment;
• Processing incoming and outgoing goods;
• Checking products for quality and quantity;
• Maintaining a safe, clean and organised workplace;
• Supporting the efficient handling of daily logistics operations.

Functie-eisen:
This position is suitable for someone who enjoys physical work and feels comfortable in a warehouse environment. You work carefully, take responsibility for the quality of your work and are willing to work different shifts.

For this position:

• You have MBO-level working and thinking ability through education or experience;
• Experience in logistics is an advantage;
• You are physically fit and willing to perform manual tasks;
• You work accurately and pay attention to quality;
• You are flexible and willing to work in a 4-shift system;
• You have a good command of either Dutch or English;
• You preferably live within 25 kilometres of the work location and have your own transportation.
